{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner's interpretation of two conditions of request 02836f9a, on the checker's question about 3d1223a1. (1) 'Never revoke an unattributed token' binds every revoker in the fork, including Workspaces' inventory sweep under R-WS-3. A token that a ForkTokens record in the unknown state may own is attributed-pending, not unattributed: the sweep must keep it (by the window and label the record stored before the create, or by the id once known), and only the ledger's listing pass may settle the record and release the token for revocation by id. R-WS-3's purpose, that no unlisted active token lingers, is preserved because the unknown record is itself the durable listing that drives that pass; the report's exemption for the sweep is not accepted. (2) 'A failed revocation stays owed by id' means: once an answer carries a token id, that id is made durable before any revoke is attempted; a storage failure while recording the held state is retried with the id still in hand; if the emergency revoke then fails, the record is held and owed by id, never unknown. R-MINT-3's allowance for an earlier record state after a storage failure covers only the case where no id was ever received; it is not a licence to discard an id the Room holds. C3 is an unambiguous defect: the keep set must be rechecked immediately before each revoke. Builder is already repairing all three with committed controls."}